# behavior: private helpers that only read a Rust tree value walk it from a field, from a parameter, through a helper chain and through a cursor without copying the tree (the crate's clone counter stays at 0), an explicit clone counts once, a child taken as an owned value counts once, a snapshot taken before the owner is replaced counts the copies the replacement needs, and a tree handed to functions declared over a reference, to a returned callable and to a walk over a reference parameter adds nothing
